==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|donjon}}, {{m|fro|dongon||castle keep}}, from {{der|fr|frk||*dungjo, *dunjon-|dungeon, bower, underground cellar}}, from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*dungijǭ}}, {{m|gem-pro|*dungō||enclosed space, vault, bower, treasury}}.

Alternate etymology traces Old French ''donjon'' to {{inh|fr|VL.||*dominio, *dominionem|lord's castle}}, from {{inh|fr|la|dominius}}, and possibly influenced by the above Germanic term.

